azgor wrote:

> [6]: If teleporting monsters can't make it to the upstair, they
> teleport to the downstair. If they can't make it there, they teleport a
> long way from you to heal up. They're supposed to be supreme evil
> opponents, not klutzes who get outfoxed by a boulder on their escape
> route. There might have to be a longer tele-timeout to balance this.
> -ekiM
> 
That would be quite unbalancing as it would make it much easier to find the 
downstairs: when you arrive on a level just stand on the upstairs while the 
teleporting monsters attack and then watch where they go to know where the 
downstairs are. At the moment you can use teleporting monsters to find the 
upstairs relatively quickly, but that only really helps if you are willing 
to do Gehennom in reverse.

OTOH making them teleport to a random location when the up stairs are 
blocked sounds a great idea. If you can't find the upstairs because they 
are under a boulder why should they help you?



